      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2004 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Bivalirudin is indicated for use as an anticoagulant in patients with unstable angina undergoing percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. Cases of intracoronary thrombosis have been reported with beta-radiation when bivalirudin is used as an anticoagulant. We report two cases of intracoronary thrombosis with gamma-radiation when bivalirudin is used."
      },
